# What code-review-graph must not index.
#
# Copy this to a project root as `.code-review-graphignore`:
#
#     cp ~/claudebase/templates/project-code-review-graphignore .code-review-graphignore
#
# This is the SIBLING of `.graphifyignore`, and writing one without the other is
# the mistake this file exists to prevent. The three graphs read three different
# ignore files and none of them falls back to another:
#
#   graphify           .graphifyignore
#   code-review-graph  .code-review-graphignore   (incremental.py:392)
#   git                .gitignore
#
# Syntax is gitignore's, and a bare `dir/` matches at any depth.


# --- What you do NOT need to list ------------------------------------------
#
# CRG indexes `git ls-files` — tracked files only. So an untracked tree is
# already invisible to it, and repeating your whole .gitignore here buys
# nothing. `DEFAULT_IGNORE_PATTERNS` (incremental.py:131) additionally covers
# node_modules, vendor, dist, build, and *.min.js.
#
# The gap this file closes is the opposite one: material that IS tracked but is
# not this project's source. Two kinds show up in practice.


# --- 1. Tracked hidden directories -----------------------------------------
#
# Harness state and tooling config, much of it tracked on purpose: an
# experiment registry under .omx/, workflows under .github/, editor settings
# under .vscode/. None of it answers a question about the code.
#
# MEASURED, and the reason the list below is explicit rather than one glob:
# a leading-dot glob does NOT catch these. On a Python repo (2026-08-10), with
# `.*/` as the only rule, `.omx/` was correctly dropped but root-level
# `.vscode/` survived with 4 nodes. Name the directories; do not rely on the
# glob alone.
.*/
.omx/
.omp/
.omd/
.claude/
.github/
.sp/
.vscode/
.idea/
.pytest_cache/


# --- 2. Tracked vendored or generated code ---------------------------------
#
# The expensive case. A repo that TRACKS a third-party tree, bundled assets, or
# generated sources hands all of it to CRG precisely because it is tracked — no
# gitignore-based exclusion can reach it. The graph then reports a healthy node
# count while describing somebody else's code.
#
# Measured on an Obsidian vault (2026-08-10), this file the only change:
# 21,865 nodes / 222 MB -> 568 nodes / 12 MB. All 21,865 came from 34 tracked
# files under `.obsidian/plugins`. The tell was `javascript` dropping out of
# the language list.
#
